Running graphics apps (e.g., ggplot2) on macos using docker images (rollinroy/r-4.5.2-arm):
Preliminaries:
  1. Install Xquartz on mac
  2. Create xinit directory:
mkdir -p ~/.xinitrc.d
  3. Create xhost config file:
cat << 'EOF' > ~/.xinitrc.d/xhost-config.sh
#!/bin/sh

xhost +127.0.0.1
xhost +localhost
xhost +$(hostname)
EOF
  4. chmod  +x  ~/.xinitrc.d/xhost-config.sh
After preliminaries:
  1.check xhost to verify authenticated networks/clients
xhost
  2. run docker image with -e option
docker run --rm -it -e DISPLAY=host.docker.internal:0 rollinroy/r-4.5.2-arm

Note: To run X apps (e.g., xclock), get the x apps:
apt-get update && apt-get install -qqy x11-apps
